// Package fixtures holds the Go fixtures of the `stuttering-name-go` tool rule.
//
// The tool must report nothing here. Each exported name either does not repeat
// the package name, or it stands behind a carve-out revive makes for itself. A
// tool upgrade that reports one of them makes the doctor mark the rule
// unusable.
package fixtures

// Fixtures is exactly the package name and no longer, so a caller writes
// `fixtures.Fixtures` and reads the word one time.
type Fixtures struct{}

// Fixturesque opens with the package name and carries a lower-case rune under
// it, so the name opens no new word there.
type Fixturesque struct{}

// FixturesLimit repeats the package name on a CONSTANT. revive reads the name
// of a type and of a function alone, so a constant reports nothing.
const FixturesLimit = 1

// FixturesValue repeats the package name on a VARIABLE, and it reports nothing
// for the reason the constant reports nothing.
var FixturesValue = 1

// PlainHolder is the receiver the method below stands on.
type PlainHolder struct{}

// FixturesMethod repeats the package name on a METHOD. A caller writes a
// method name under the value it calls it on and never under the package, so
// revive reads no method name.
func (p PlainHolder) FixturesMethod() {}

// fixturesHelper repeats the package name and is unexported, so no caller
// outside the package can write it at all.
func fixturesHelper() int { return FixturesLimit }

// PlainBuild calls the unexported name above, and it opens with no package
// name of its own.
func PlainBuild() int { return fixturesHelper() }

// The block below holds the inline suppression the rule body names. It is the
// one way to exempt an exported name, and the name it stands above repeats the
// package name in the shape the failing fixture reports.

//revive:disable-next-line:exported
type FixturesSuppressed struct{}

// The declaration below carries NO doc comment, and a blank line stands under
// this prose so that this prose is not its doc comment. revive reports it
// under the `comments` category, which `missing-docs-go` owns and this rule's
// filter drops. A filter that stopped reading the category would report it
// here and fail this fixture.

type Undocumented struct{}
